B.afA=new A.b3("Win (checked at the end of a round, from round 4): Military \u2014 hold your capital + 4 Key points (rival capital 2, sea Key Region 2, neutral nation 1) for 2 rounds; Economic \u2014 Dominance Score 79+ across Trade, Finance, Investment and Resilience (each 0\u201325; 3 of them at 15+) at the end of a round; trade routes and chokepoints count toward Trade; Tech \u2014 research Level 5; same-round ties: more Key Regions, then more Prestige; exact ties share the win. No round-8 cutoff: from the end of round 12 a Prestige lead of 3+ ends the game (most Prestige wins; tie: income), otherwise overtime runs to the end of round 16, when most Prestige wins (Quick Match only: Top Score after round 8).\nPrestige: +1 a round per National Objective held (\u2691); Theater Review +3/+2/+1; \u22121 for a turn without pressure on a rival; standoffs.\nAttacks: Armor and air may attack again after a capture, but a power takes at most 2 rival regions a turn, and a power loses at most 2 regions a round (then its regions are safe until the round ends).\nCrisis (Protest \u2192 Threat \u2192 Mobilize \u2192 Strike): when a rival attacks your region, Partner, Objective or home theater, reaches research Level 4+ or plays Corner the Market, you may Protest. The actor makes a Threat (commits a card) or blinks (the action is called off, \u22121/+1); you Mobilize (commit) or blink (\u22122/+2); at the Strike each may add a card and both reveal. Each card counts its number (1-3, top-left corner); Countermeasures makes their highest card count 0. Higher total +6/\u22126; a challenger win cancels the action; a tie lets it go ahead.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
